# Cloud credentials for the web application.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local development. Without them Noto
# runs local-first and complete — documents, search, Quick Note and the dock all
# work — and the sign-in screen says there is no account service rather than
# offering a form that cannot succeed.
#
# These are build-time values: Vite inlines them into the bundle. For the
# deployed application that build happens on Cloudflare, not in GitHub Actions,
# so the same three go in the `noto-web` project under Settings -> Build ->
# Variables and secrets. Setting them anywhere else configures a build nobody
# deploys; see docs/deployment/website.md.
#
# All three are public by design — they are served to every visitor inside the
# bundle. Row Level Security, not secrecy, is what protects the data. The
# `service_role` key and the Turnstile *secret* are not public, belong to
# Supabase's function secrets, and must never appear here.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-key

# Without this, sign-in still works and creating an account is not offered:
# the Edge Function fails closed on a missing token, so a build with no sitekey
# cannot create accounts and should not pretend it can.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=your-turnstile-sitekey
